<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Changchub Gyaltsen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1302">1302</a>–<a href="/years/1364">1364</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Tai Situ Changchub Gyaltsen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Changchub Gyaltsen was the myriarch of Phagmodru who overthrew the Mongol-backed Sakya regime in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> in the 1350s. Founder of the Phagmodrupa dynasty, he revived Tibetan traditions of the old empire, reorganised the country into districts under fortress governors and issued a new law code, restoring native rule after the decline of the Yuan.</p></div>
